<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89590" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσκηδής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῆδος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bringing into alliance</i> or <i>kindred</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξεινοσύνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					21.35
				</span></i>
			: but perh. <i>kindly</i>, as in <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.588
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>connected</i> by marriage, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.136
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσκηδέες</span>”
				<i>kinsfolk,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					7.444
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Theaet.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.717
			</span></i> (but perh. <i>careworn</i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
